(
    title: "Escape from the Mindmaster",
    developer: Some("Dennis Caswell"),
    description: Some("A first-person 3D maze across six levels of an alien ship — startling depth for 1982, possible only because the Supercharger streamed each level from cassette. Find the shaped pegs, slot them into matching sockets to open the way out, and keep moving: the Alien Stalker roams every maze and cannot be killed. Between levels, mini-games of memory and reflex feed the score, and later mazes add forcefields and one-way doors. Shipped as a four-load tape; the beta was titled Labyrinth."),
